@startuml
title P1 Main UI, Local Self-Test and Capture - key flows

skinparam shadowing false

actor User
participant "Main window / tray" as Shell
participant "Capture service" as Capture
database "Temp media store" as Temp
participant "Output path" as Output

== Try locally - no upload ==

User -> Shell: Open Try locally
User -> Shell: Pick input/output and choose builtin cue\nor Record 5 seconds

alt Builtin cue
  Shell -> Output: Play builtin cue on selected output
else Microphone self-test
  Shell -> Capture: Start explicit local recording
  Capture -> Shell: Request microphone permission
  alt Permission granted
    Capture -> Capture: Capture mono PCM and update level meter
    Capture -> Temp: Write app-private temp file
    Capture -> Output: Play back through the same clip output path
  else Permission denied
    Capture -> Shell: Show honest denial guidance
    note right
    File playback and builtin cue remain available.
    No hidden background capture is allowed.
    end note
  end
end

User -> Shell: Delete or close self-test
Shell -> Temp: Delete temporary media

note over Shell,Temp
No upload session, control token, coordinator call,
or transmission request occurs anywhere in Try locally.
end note

newpage

title P1 Main UI, Local Self-Test and Capture - record and send

actor User
participant "Main window / tray" as Shell2
participant "Capture service" as Capture2
database "Temp media store" as Temp2
participant "Upload API" as Upload
participant "Transmission API" as Tx
participant "History/presence model" as Model

== Record and send ==

User -> Shell2: Press Record or toggle hotkey
Shell2 -> Capture2: Begin capture
Capture2 -> Shell2: Visible + audible recording indication
Capture2 -> Capture2: Update level meter\nand enforce 180 second limit

alt User presses Esc
  Shell2 -> Capture2: Cancel recording
  Capture2 -> Temp2: Delete temp draft
  Shell2 -> User: Show cancelled state
else User stops normally
  Shell2 -> Capture2: Finalize draft
  Capture2 -> Temp2: Persist temp draft
  Shell2 -> Upload: Create upload session
  Upload --> Shell2: Scoped upload token
  Shell2 -> Upload: Upload draft bytes
  alt Upload or coordinator failure
    Upload --> Shell2: Failed or unavailable
    Shell2 -> User: Show honest unsent state
    note right
    A finalized user draft is promoted from capture temp storage
    to durable app-private draft storage and survives restart until
    retry, confirmed upload, or explicit delete.
    Self-test recordings never enter this lifecycle.
    UI must not claim "sent".
    end note
  else Media ready
    Upload --> Shell2: media_id
    Shell2 -> Tx: Create transmission\naudience + delivery + play here
    Tx --> Model: Receipts, history, presence updates
    Model --> Shell2: Render accepted -> played\nor missed/failure reasons
    Shell2 -> Temp2: Delete draft after confirmed upload
  end
end

note bottom
Capture tasks own permission, meter, cue, temp-file and hotkey behavior.
Integration tasks start at upload-session creation and receipt rendering.
end note

@enduml
